}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Hesperia}}|area_km2=40056|population_census=2,369,634|population_census_year=[[2025 Baliscan census|2025]]|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Neapolitan language|Neapolitan]], [[Baliscano]], [[w:Judaeo-Spanish|Ladino]], [[Mozarabic]]|cctld=.blo|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|mapsize=280px|population_census_rank=20th}}'''Basilisco''' ({{lang-bl|Basilisca}}), alternatively spelled '''Basilisca''', is a mountainous coastal [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of the [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Hesperia]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders the [[Strait of Sicania]] to the north, [[Tartessia]] to the southeast, [[Trás-as-Montanyas]] to the southwest, and [[Aprica]] to the west. The administrative seat and most populous commune within the region is [[Cordova]].

The climate of Basilisco is relatively similar to the meteorological conditions of the [[Algarves]] and the wayward coast of [[Sicania]]. The high areas of the region receive more rain than the coastal areas, the same thing that happens in the northern area with respect to the southern area. Temperatures remain stable throughout the year, with the highest during the summer. The phenomenon of horizontal rain is very important in it [[Fortaleza Ecological Park]], where the water contained in the mists is deposited, creating a dense laurel forest.

Basilisco is the 13th-largest region by area, with an area of {{convert|40056|km2}}, and is the 20th-most populous, with an recorded population of 2,369,634 people in 2025. The majority of Basilisco's residents live in the metropolitan area of [[Cordova]], which is also the regional center of transportation, business, and industry located in the [[Taro Valley]]. 

